<!--
    Test dataset for AllergiesSectionTest.
    Allergies are stored in the allergy table (PK: allergy_id) with reactions in the
    allergy_reaction table (FK: allergy_id). getAllergies(patient) returns ALL allergies
    for a patient regardless of visit, so allergies are patient-scoped, not visit-scoped.

    Concept IDs 7001-7006 to avoid conflicts with vitalsSectionTestDataset (5001-5009)
    and diagnosesSectionTestDataset (6001-6003).
    Visit IDs 301+ to avoid conflicts with vitals (101-106) and diagnoses (201-204).
    Allergy/allergy_reaction IDs 301+ for the same reason.

    Patient 2 (from standardTestDataset) — 2 allergies:
      Allergy 301 — Penicillin (DRUG), severity=Severe, reactions: Rash + Nausea
      Allergy 302 — Peanuts (FOOD), severity=Mild, reaction: Rash

    Visit 301 — for patient 2 (has allergies)
    Visit 302 — for patient 7 (no allergies, empty-list test)
-->
